@startuml storage_concurrency
' Style and layout settings
!theme plain
skinparam rectangle {
  shadowing false
  borderRadius 10
}
skinparam interface {
  shadowing false
}

' The IStorageBackend interface is clean and has no knowledge of locking.
interface "IStorageBackend" as IBackend {
  +write(key, data)
  +read(key)
  +exists(key)
  +remove(key)
}

class "InMemoryBackend" implements IBackend {
  ' Concrete implementation for the L1 cache.
}

' The decorator implements the same interface and adds the locking behavior.
class "ConcurrentStorageDecorator" implements IBackend {
  -backend: IStorageBackend
  -lock: internal_lock_object
  +write(key, data)
  +read(key)
  +exists(key)
  +remove(key)
}

note right of ConcurrentStorageDecorator
  **Decorator for L1 Cache**
  The decorator wraps the shared
  `InMemoryBackend` to serialize
  access from parallel workers,
  ensuring the L1 cache is thread-safe.
end note

ConcurrentStorageDecorator o-- "1" InMemoryBackend : wraps

@enduml